-- title:
--   Gotzmann maximal growth: general linear form regular in degrees ≥ m
-- statement:
--   Let $n,m$ be natural numbers and $K$ an infinite field, and let $J$ be an ideal of the polynomial ring $K[X_0,\dots,X_n]$ in $n+1$ variables indexed by `Fin (n + 1)`. Assume $J$ is generated by forms of a single degree $m$: there is a set $s$ of polynomials, each homogeneous of degree $m$, with $J = \operatorname{span} s$. Write, for $d \in \mathbb{N}$, `piece J d` for the $K$-vector space obtained from the submodule of forms of degree $d$ by quotienting out those forms that lie in $J$, i.e. $K[X]_d/(J \cap K[X]_d)$. Assume the Hilbert function of $J$ grows maximally from degree $m$ to degree $m+1$: $\dim_K(\mathrm{piece}\ J\ (m+1)) = \mathrm{Nat.macaulayPow}\ m\ (\dim_K(\mathrm{piece}\ J\ m))$, where [`Nat.macaulayPow`](def/Nat_MacaulayPow.html#L7) is Macaulay's upper pseudo-power, given by the recursion `macaulayPow 0 a = 0` and, writing $k$ for the greatest $k \le a + d + 1$ with $\binom{k}{d+1} \le a$, `macaulayPow (d+1) a` $= \binom{k+1}{d+2} + \mathrm{macaulayPow}\ d\ (a - \binom{k}{d+1})$. Then there is a nonzero polynomial $G \in K[X_0,\dots,X_n]$ such that for every $a \colon \mathrm{Fin}\ (n+1) \to K$ with $G(a) \ne 0$, every $k \ge m$ and every form $f$ of degree $k$, the relation $\bigl(\sum_i a_i X_i\bigr) f \in J$ forces $f \in J$.
--
--   This is the colon-ideal half of Gotzmann's theory of ideals of maximal growth: for an ideal generated in a single degree $m$ whose Hilbert function attains Macaulay's bound in the next degree, a general linear form $\ell_a = \sum_i a_i X_i$ is a non-zero-divisor on $K[X]/J$ in all degrees $\ge m$, the genericity being expressed by non-vanishing of one fixed polynomial $G$ (whence the hypothesis that $K$ be infinite). It is used in the construction of the Hilbert functor and of sections of maximal growth on projective space, and through those in the persistence statements about powers of variables multiplying into $J$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_exists_forall_eval_ne_zero_mem_of_mul_mem_of_finrank_piece_succ_eq_macaulayPow.lean

